    {
      "category": "polarity",
      "components": ["U6"],
      "pins": ["U6.1", "U6.2", "U7.1"],
      "nets": ["BAT+", "Net-(U6-A)"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the SS2040FL U6 is drawn with its anode (pin 1, triangle base) tied to the BAT+ node and its cathode (pin 2, bar) tied to the battery positive U7.1 (+).",
      "expected": "The specification requires the opposite orientation: battery positive feeds the anode and the cathode drives BAT+ ('U6 (SS2040FL) anode→cathode → BAT+', 'anode on battery (via U7), cathode on BAT+'), so that the cell can power BAT+ while USB/adapter 5 V cannot back-feed into the unprotected 18650.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EthernetAndPower.kicad_sch: U6 SS2040FL pin1 (anode) → BAT+, pin2 (cathode) → U7.1 '+'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "pin 1 → Net-(U6-A) → U6 (SS2040FL) anode→cathode → BAT+ ... anode on battery (via U7), cathode on BAT+"}
      ],
      "impact": "Reversed isolation diode: the 18650 cannot power the BAT+ rail (board dead on battery), and any USB/DC 5 V present on BAT+ forward-biases U6 into the raw cell, charging an unprotected 18650 with no charge management — a safety hazard.",
      "confidence": 0.5
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet C1 (the boost-converter input bulk capacitor at the Display_Power_Switch node, in parallel with C2) is marked 0.1uF/16V.",
      "expected": "The specification's component table lists Meshinger C1 as 1 µF/25 V (the PDI 'C2 default' bulk cap mapped to C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10).",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "EPD_Driver.kicad_sch: C1 0.1uF/16V on the L1 input / Display_Power_Switch node"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V"}
      ],
      "impact": "Input bulk decoupling of the EPD boost stage is ten times smaller than intended (and the voltage rating differs), which can degrade boost-converter regulation / increase input ripple during e-paper refresh.",
      "confidence": 0.45
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Two deviations from the documented reference design are visible: the battery-isolation Schottky U6 appears reverse-connected (anode on BAT+ instead of on the cell), which would block battery power and risk charging an unprotected 18650 from USB/DC input; and the EPD boost input bulk cap C1 is populated as 0.1 µF/16 V rather than the specified 1 µF/25 V. Other spec-noted items (SPI bit-bang labels, RJ45 open item, S1-as-reset, barrel-jack battery disconnect) match the drawing and are not reported."
}

